- Story & Context: The legendary closing track of the scene, detailing the mythical final day of Station 4-Alpha when the keepers vanished, leaving only a locked broadcast room playing an automated 11/8 brass loop on infinite repeat. Fishermen still claim the signal bounces off icebergs, carrying a ghost-like, heavily reverbed trumpet solo that bends pitch as the ocean currents shift. The music builds from a solitary, weeping brass moan into a towering, maximalist Balkan pop crescendo that abruptly cuts to the sound of open wind and ticking clockwork. "The logbook is full of blank hours, but the horns will finish the shift for us," echoes the final chorus.
